<BaseLayout title="About" description="Meet Donald Chinhuru: senior software engineer, payments and mobile specialist, technical lead and active PMP."><div class="wrap"><section class="page-intro about-intro"><span class="eyebrow">THE ENGINEER BEHIND THE WORK</span><h1>I like the parts<br /><span class="muted">that connect.</span></h1><p>I’m Donald Chinhuru, a software engineer based in Zimbabwe. My work sits where payments, mobile experiences and business operations meet.</p></section><section class="about-story"><div class="identity-card"><div class="identity-monogram">dc<span>.</span></div><h2>Donald Chinhuru</h2><p>Senior software engineer</p><div class="identity-divider"></div><span class="eyebrow">PROJECT MANAGEMENT PROFESSIONAL</span><strong>PMP · earned 2024</strong><span>Active certification</span><a href="/contact/" class="text-link">Get in touch <Arrow diagonal /></a></div><div class="prose"><h2>From the terminal to the business behind it.</h2><p>My interests don’t stop at a working screen. I want to understand what happens next: the payment message, the approval, the business record, and the tools people need to operate the system.</p><p>That has taken me from Android POS engineering and Flutter banking apps to Java services, Angular portals and Frappe/ERPNext custom applications. It is also why I build reusable tools — including Vant Flow and the WCE ecosystem — when a problem keeps repeating.</p><p>In my work roles, I’ve led mobile, fullstack and systems engineering. On my own projects, I take the product from its first idea through architecture and implementation. I care about making both the software and its reasoning understandable.</p><p>I also build Kinetiframe, a native Android animation studio combining frame-by-frame drawing with reusable characters and performances.</p><p>I write about the practical details along the way: dynamic forms, local chatbot development, payment integrations and the engineering decisions behind them.</p></div></section>
